[31m-## Overview[m
[31m-[m
[31m-WasteVision AI is designed to help a project team build and manage a[m
[31m-computer-vision system for identifying waste, including small and[m
[31m-fragmented waste pieces. The workspace brings dataset preparation, image[m
[31m-annotation, model training, evaluation, prediction testing, experiment[m
[31m-records, model versions, documentation, and team task management into[m
[31m-one application.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The broader project objective is to investigate identifying small waste[m
[31m-fragments---potentially around **1--2 cm**---such as pieces of plastic,[m
[31m-glass, metal, paper, and other waste. Actual minimum detectable size and[m
[31m-accuracy depend on image resolution, camera distance, lighting, object[m
[31m-visibility, dataset quality, and the trained model. These capabilities[m
[31m-must be validated experimentally; they should not be assumed from the[m
[31m-interface alone.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Project goals[m
[31m-[m
[31m--   Organize image datasets and dataset versions.[m
[31m--   Label images and, where supported, draw object bounding boxes.[m
[31m--   Validate annotations and prepare data for training.[m
[31m--   Configure and monitor computer-vision training jobs.[m
[31m--   Evaluate models with task-appropriate metrics.[m
[31m--   Test predictions on new images or videos when supported.[m
[31m--   Keep model checkpoints and experiment results associated with their[m
[31m-    training runs.[m
[31m--   Coordinate work through a shared team workspace and Kanban board.[m
[31m--   Restrict project data to authenticated, authorized team members.[m
[31m--   Provide a web interface that can be deployed independently of[m
[31m-    long-running model-training workloads.[m
