[31m-### Classification versus object detection[m
[31m-[m
[31m--   **Image classification** predicts a category for an entire image. It[m
[31m-    does not identify the location of each object within that image.[m
[31m--   **Object detection** predicts both a category and a location,[m
[31m-    commonly represented by a bounding box, for each detected object.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-If the goal is to locate several small waste fragments in one image, an[m
[31m-object-detection approach and suitable bounding-box annotations are[m
[31m-generally required. The final choice depends on the existing training[m
[31m-pipeline and project requirements.[m
